  "title": "Kruibeke Bazel Rupelmonde (Belgium): a controlled flood area for flood safety and nature protection",
  "summary": "The Kruibeke Bazel Rupelmonde (KBR) Controlled Flood Area is a key part of Belgium's Sigma Plan, providing flood protection for 20000 hectares in the Scheldt Estuary while also offering restored habitats and recreation. It proved its efficacy for the first time during the strong tide event of January 2018, offering a useful buffer area and preventing a dangerous flooding. The Kruibeke Bazel Rupelmonde (KBR) Controlled Flood Area (CFA) is a key component of the Belgian Sigma Plan for the Scheldt Estuary . The Sigma Plan is an integrated flood protection plan that combines dikes, seawalls and flood areas to protect approximately 20,000 hectares of land from flooding.",
